// The Dorado backplane: every board, wired together by signal name.
//
// Generated by tools/sil_backplane.py --emit. DO NOT EDIT.
// Source: <Board>.bp in chm/sil -- PARC's own statement of which nets
// leave each board, cross-checked against the .wl and the .nl pair.
//
// Boards connect BY NAME, not by pin: the backplane is not
// straight-through (the BaseBoard drives CLK.ph' from C16 into ProcH's
// C9), and 182 pin positions carry different nets on different boards.
//
// Each board exports its CONTRIBUTION to a net as `<net>__drv` and this
// module ORs them -- MECL open emitters wired together, in a form that
// synthesises. No `inout`, no multiply-driven net.
//
// Configuration: ContA ContB ProcH ProcL
// 205 internal nets (38 with several contributors), 169 top-level ports.

